    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **11 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on the owner so that creating (and reading back) an owner returns the name formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field exposed in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping that computes the field from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause the create endpoint (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) and the read endpoint (`getOwner`) both serialize the owner via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, the computed `displayName` is now returned consistently. The acceptance test `Cp05Tests` and all existing tests pass.",
